# oracle: pair mdpd with mdpd/rhosum (many-body DPD, hybrid/overlay) and fix mvv/dpd, a cut-down of examples/PACKAGES/dpd-meso/mdpd/in.mdpd (a thin fcc film of about 3800 atoms, 200 steps)
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native max error 3.2e-11 (thermo) and 3.6e-9 (per-atom, scale max(1,|x|)) under vitest (Node 24) and under Node 20 with a rolldown bundle (3.2e-11 thermo, 3.6e-9 per-atom). The densities of mdpd/rhosum and the per-pair draws follow native's order step by step.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=0
# rel loosened from 1e-10 after the core RanPark uniform became AM*seed (native src/random_park.cpp, b332f28, bit-exact now): the random stream is the same, but the 200-step run amplifies ulp differences in the pair draws; press at step 200 moved from 3.2e-11 to 3.5e-10 relative (the full oracle run failed at 1e-10)
units 		        lj
dimension	        3
boundary	        p p p
neighbor	        0.3 bin
neigh_modify        every 1 delay 0 check yes

atom_style	        mdpd
comm_modify vel yes

region     mdpd     block -12 12 -6 6 -6 6 units box
create_box          1 mdpd

lattice             fcc 6
region     film     block -10 10 -4 4 -2 2 units box
create_atoms        1 region film

pair_style          hybrid/overlay mdpd/rhosum mdpd 1.0 1.0 9872598
pair_coeff          1 1 mdpd/rhosum  0.75
pair_coeff          1 1 mdpd         -40 25 18.0 1.0 0.75
mass                1 1.0

compute             mythermo all temp
thermo              100
thermo_style        custom step temp pe ke etotal press
thermo_modify       temp mythermo
thermo_modify       flush yes
thermo_modify       format float %.15g

velocity            all create 1.0 38497 loop local dist gaussian

fix         mvv     all mvv/dpd

timestep            0.01
run                 200
